<worksheet >
    <title>MD-1 Matrix Operations</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete all four parts. 
      Complete any three parts to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <introduction><p>Given the following matrices:
          <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="3">
          <mrow>P=\begin{bmatrix} 2 &amp; 1 \\ 1 &amp; 2 \end{bmatrix}, 
            Q=\begin{bmatrix} -1 &amp; 2 \\ 3 &amp; -1 \end{bmatrix}, 
            R=\begin{bmatrix} 3 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 3 \end{bmatrix}, 
            S=\begin{bmatrix} 1 &amp; 2 &amp; -2 \\ 3 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 \end{bmatrix}</mrow>
        </md> 
            Compute the following matrices, if possible.  If the computation is not 
            possible, explain why.</p></introduction>
      <task><statement><p><m>(PQ)^T</m></p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p><m>Q(P+R)</m></p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p><m>S^2</m></p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p><m>P^{-1}R</m></p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>